# Quorian

## Lore

The Quorians are a warrior race summoned from an alien world by the Dwarves during the Elf-Dwarf War: tall, broad and muscular, with pupilless reddish eyes, dusty blue-purple skin and rope-like tendril hair often tied back in a bundled ponytail. Aggressive yet disciplined, they rarely engage in senseless bloodshed and hold life in high regard - unless it is a Gosai''s - and many wander as mercenaries.

They are deeply superstitious and take their rare dream-visions very seriously, so Quorian shamans, Psi-Mystics and above all Oneiromancers are revered as interpreters of dreams. Within a year of the first vision a young Quorian leaves the family wandercamp and may never return. Their sense of personal honor is easily insulted and quickly settled by duel or brawl, and their Healing Factor makes them foolhardy: retreat is close to taboo, and many would rather die in a losing battle than run. Displaced for generations, many Quorians search the Megaverse for a way back to a homeworld nobody can find, and Rifts Earth, with its thousand Rifts, has drawn hundreds of them.

**Alignment:** Any, but lean very heavily toward the honorable alignments - Principled (25%), Scrupulous (35%) and Aberrant evil (30%).

**Size:** 6-7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m). **Weight:** 200-300 lbs (90 to 135 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 50-60 years.

**Habitat:** Largely the Baalgor Wastelands on Palladium, otherwise anywhere. On Rifts Earth they are found near places of magic, ley lines and dimensional portals; at least a hundred serve the Splugorth on Atlantis as assassins, elite warriors and spies, and they have been reported at Tolkeen, Calgary, the Detroit-Windsor and St. Louis Rifts, the Magic Zone, the Federation of Magic, the Yucatan and the British Isles.

## GM Notes

Their enemies are the Gosai, Giants, Trolls, Ogres, Orcs and anybody who interferes with their quest to go home. They count the Eandroth, Dragonmen and humans as allies, stand off from Dwarves and Elves, and are indifferent to most others. On Rifts Earth they get along with traditional Native Americans, Psi-Stalkers, Mystics, Nature Spirits and O.C.C.s like their own.
